# Physical animation profiles for a person (ae3d.physanim.profiles_read).
# A profile starts with every body driven at the anchors' own strength and
# drawn at weight 0; each line sets one body (body) or it and every body
# below it (below): its mode (kinematic, driven or simulated), its anchor's
# hertz, force and torque (0 the anchors' own, unbounded), and its weight.

# Arms hanging loose: pulled weakly onto the animation and drawn more than
# half from their bodies, so they swing with what the body does.
profile loose_arms
below ShoulderL driven hertz 2 weight 0.6
below ShoulderR driven hertz 2 weight 0.6

# Arms moved exactly as animated, pushing what they meet: a guard, a carry.
profile stiff_arms
below ShoulderL kinematic
below ShoulderR kinematic

# A soft trunk: the spine, chest, neck and arms held weakly, so a blow
# carries them further before they come back.
profile soft_trunk
below Spine driven hertz 1.5
